  "title": "fix: publish relative-path support to npm",
  "user": { "login": "konard", "id": 1431904, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard", "html_url": "https://github.com/konard", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false },
  "body": "Fixes #40.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe issue reproduced the relative-path/cwd failure already fixed by #36, but npm still served `gh-upload-log@0.8.2`. GitHub had releases `v0.8.3` and `v0.9.0`; neither version existed in the npm registry.\n\nArchived release logs show why:\n\n- The workflow ran Node 20 and attempted to install npm 12, which failed with `EBADENGINE`.\n- Both npm publishes then failed with `E404`.\n- command-stream returned `{ code: 1 }`, but the release script only used `try/catch`, so it printed success and created GitHub releases anyway.\n- `gh-upload-log --version` was hardcoded to `0.1.0`, hiding the installed package version during diagnosis.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nAt investigation time:\n\n```text\n$ npm view gh-upload-log version\n0.8.2\n\n$ gh-upload-log --version\n0.1.0\n```\n\nRelease run [32512441957](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-upload-log/actions/runs/32512441957) shows npm 12 reject Node 20 at log lines 3841-3846, npm publish fail at lines 3948-3970, and the script immediately print `Published gh-upload-log@0.8.3`. Run [32588725260](https://github.com/link-foundation/gh-upload-log/actions/runs/32588725260) repeated the false success for `0.9.0`.\n\n## Solution\n\n- Use Node 24 and npm `^11.5.1` in both publishing jobs, satisfying npm trusted publishing's Node >=22.14/npm >=11.5.1 requirements.\n- Validate command-stream exit codes during npm setup, git pull, and package publishing.\n- Retry failed publishes three times, then fail the job; set the `published` output only after a verified zero exit code.\n- Make release helpers import-safe and dependency-injectable for offline unit tests.\n- Read the CLI version from the installed `package.json` instead of hardcoding it.\n- Normalize the package repository URL and add a patch changeset so the corrected flow publishes a new npm version containing the existing relative-path fix.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n- `test/release.test.js`: failed publish results retry and reject; a later zero exit succeeds; both release paths use the compatible toolchain; npm setup rejects `EBADENGINE`.\n- `test/cli.test.js`: `--version` must match `package.json`.\n- Existing `test/path-handling.test.js`: bare, `./`, `../`, `~/`, and absolute paths resolve consistently, including a mocked cwd mutation during repository upload.\n\nManual issue-shaped verification used a sparse 40.29 MB `hive-telegram-bot.log`. Both `hive-telegram-bot.log` and `./hive-telegram-bot.log` resolved to the same absolute input, content hash, repository path, and `.log.txt` stored filename in repository dry mode.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bun test` — 106 pass, 0 fail\n- `bun run check` — ESLint, Prettier, and file-size checks pass\n- changeset validation against `origin/main` passes\n- `npm pack --dry-run --json` includes `src/package-version.js` and `src/cli.js`\n- `origin/main` is already an ancestor of this branch\n\n## Case study\n\n[`docs/case-studies/issue-40/README.md`](docs/case-studies/issue-40/README.md) records the registry/tag mismatch, release-log evidence, root cause, fix, and residual post-merge publication check.\n",
